00:21:52.215 --> 00:21:54.576
- Time, how many people in the room

00:21:54.576 --> 00:21:56.826
would say they're too busy?

00:21:57.836 --> 00:21:59.169
Not busy enough?

00:22:00.365 --> 00:22:02.998
That's a politically unpopular
place to put your hand

00:22:02.998 --> 00:22:05.339
but God bless you for putting
your hand up over there.

00:22:05.339 --> 00:22:06.697
(audience laughs)

00:22:06.697 --> 00:22:10.354
The truth of the matter
is thinking about time

00:22:10.354 --> 00:22:13.307
as something to be managed,

00:22:13.307 --> 00:22:16.358
whether it's how long, for
those of you who are seniors,

00:22:16.358 --> 00:22:17.507
I'm sure you'll ask the question,

00:22:17.507 --> 00:22:20.496
"How long will I do my first job.

00:22:20.496 --> 00:22:21.959
"How long, will I stay in my job

00:22:21.959 --> 00:22:25.072
"six months, a year, five years?

00:22:25.072 --> 00:22:28.353
"How long before I decide
whether I really like my career?

00:22:28.353 --> 00:22:31.655
"How long before I really like my major?

00:22:31.655 --> 00:22:34.497
"How am I really managing my time?"

00:22:34.497 --> 00:22:36.838
I got involved with a
lot of extracurriculars.

00:22:36.838 --> 00:22:39.032
The one that broke the bank for me

00:22:39.032 --> 00:22:41.755
was becoming published of the Advocate.

00:22:41.755 --> 00:22:43.469
I'm not even sure why I did it.

00:22:43.469 --> 00:22:44.911
Really, I'm not sure why I did it.

00:22:44.911 --> 00:22:47.586
Was another resume
build, I was already busy

00:22:47.586 --> 00:22:49.216
with football and the Crimson.

00:22:49.216 --> 00:22:51.034
But I did it, and then,

00:22:51.034 --> 00:22:54.867
time management really
got into my vocabulary.

00:22:55.736 --> 00:22:57.157
I really did have the management,

00:22:57.157 --> 00:22:58.975
and I don't even manage it--

00:22:58.975 --> 00:23:02.193
I started skipping class, I
already sort of confessed to that.

00:23:02.193 --> 00:23:05.725
But managing time, even
amongst the extracurriculars,

00:23:05.725 --> 00:23:08.233
got to be a big deal.

00:23:08.233 --> 00:23:10.866
Today, I actually keep
a spreadsheet, a budget.

00:23:10.866 --> 00:23:12.810
These are all the things
I'm going to do in my life,

00:23:12.810 --> 00:23:15.443
here's how much time is
budgeted to and then allocated.

00:23:15.443 --> 00:23:18.193
I record everything into Outlook,

00:23:19.831 --> 00:23:22.945
I still have a macro that
spits it out in Excel,

00:23:22.945 --> 00:23:25.516
and I do budget versus actual comparisons.

00:23:25.516 --> 00:23:28.797
It's a little different
since I've "retired"

00:23:28.797 --> 00:23:31.680
but at Microsoft, I could tell you

00:23:31.680 --> 00:23:35.651
I was going to have 12
one-on-ones with Harry this year,

00:23:35.651 --> 00:23:38.180
and then I would track
them, how many did I have?

00:23:38.180 --> 00:23:41.628
I was going to spend
10 hours a year talking

00:23:41.628 --> 00:23:44.700
to customers over the
telephone versus in person,

00:23:44.700 --> 00:23:46.518
and I just measure everything

00:23:46.518 --> 00:23:49.402
'cause I think time is so, so important.

00:23:49.402 --> 00:23:50.656
When you have enough success that

00:23:50.656 --> 00:23:54.365
what you need to do is
peddle fast, that's good.

00:23:54.365 --> 00:23:55.890
A lot of people try to peddle fast

00:23:55.890 --> 00:23:58.879
before they have anything
that's worth peddling,

00:23:58.879 --> 00:24:01.679
and a lot of other
people never peddle fast.

00:24:01.679 --> 00:24:03.790
So, it's kind of a life lesson.

00:24:03.790 --> 00:24:07.957
Get a good idea, and then work
like hell to make it popular.

